WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:17.135
When Oliver awoke the next morning, he was surprised to find a new pair of shoes on the

2
00:00:17.175 --> 00:00:18.196
floor next to his bed.

3
00:00:19.297 --> 00:00:21.598
He hoped this meant that Fagin was going to release him.

4
00:00:22.598 --> 00:00:25.360
But his hope disappeared as soon as he sat down to breakfast.

5
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.663
"You're going to be taken to the residence of Bill Sikes tonight, my dear," said Fagin.

6
00:00:33.012 --> 00:00:34.072
"To to stay there, sir?"

7
00:00:34.473 --> 00:00:35.613
Oliver asked anxiously.

8
00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:37.854
"No, no, my dear.

9
00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:40.075
We wouldn't like to lose you.

10
00:00:41.175 --> 00:00:42.356
Don't be afraid, Oliver.

11
00:00:43.416 --> 00:00:44.657
You'll come back to us again.

12
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:47.978
We wouldn't be so cruel as to send you away.

13
00:00:47.998 --> 00:00:49.679
Oh no."

14
00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:53.760
The old man was stooping over the fire, toasting a piece of bread.

15
00:00:54.861 --> 00:00:58.602
He turned around and looked at Oliver as if he knew that the boy wanted to escape.

16
00:00:58.622 --> 00:01:01.964
"I suppose you want to know why you're going to Bill's."

17
00:01:03.784 --> 00:01:05.245
Fagin fixed his eyes on Oliver.

18
00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.926
"Yes, sir."

19
00:01:06.946 --> 00:01:09.188
"Why do you think you're going?"

20
00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:12.450
"Indeed I don't know, sir," replied Oliver.

21
00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.952
"Bah!" said Fagin, turning back to the fire.

22
00:01:15.972 --> 00:01:18.494
"Wait until Bill tells you then."

23
00:01:19.655 --> 00:01:22.677
For the rest of the day, Fagin was in a sour and silent mood.

24
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:25.459
In the evening he prepared to go out.

25
00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.281
"You may burn a candle," he said, putting one on the table.

26
00:01:30.322 --> 00:01:32.744
"And here's a book for you to read until they come to fetch you.

27
00:01:33.848 --> 00:01:34.248
Good night."

28
00:01:34.268 --> 00:01:35.729
"Good night!"

29
00:01:36.169 --> 00:01:37.129
Oliver said softly.

30
00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:40.350
Fagin started to leave, but then he turned around.

31
00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.350
"Take heed, Oliver!

32
00:01:43.351 --> 00:01:44.931
Bill Sikes is a dangerous man.

33
00:01:46.031 --> 00:01:47.572
Do whatever he tells you to do.

34
00:01:48.672 --> 00:01:51.233
And no matter what happens, say nothing."

35
00:01:52.273 --> 00:01:53.513
The old man disappeared.

36
00:01:55.274 --> 00:01:59.435
Oliver sat with his head in his hands, pondering with a trembling heart the words he had just

37
00:01:59.475 --> 00:02:02.996
heard. At last he picked up the book and began to read.

38
00:02:04.116 --> 00:02:07.017
It was a history of the lives and trials of great criminals.

39
00:02:08.198 --> 00:02:10.759
And it was so frightening that Oliver slammed the book shut.

40
00:02:11.859 --> 00:02:13.020
He heard a rustling sound.

41
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.681
"Who's there?"

42
00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.642
he cried, catching sight of a figure standing by the door.

43
00:02:17.662 --> 00:02:20.783
"Only me," said a tremulous voice.

44
00:02:21.984 --> 00:02:25.305
Oliver raised the candle and saw Nancy, looking pale and ill.

45
00:02:25.325 --> 00:02:27.326
"Has anything happened?"

46
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:28.226
asked Oliver.

47
00:02:28.246 --> 00:02:29.987
"Can I help you?

48
00:02:30.967 --> 00:02:31.848
I will if I can."

49
00:02:32.972 --> 00:02:33.973
"God forgive me!"

50
00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:35.234
exclaimed the young woman.

51
00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.635
"What? Why?"

52
00:02:38.696 --> 00:02:40.257
Nancy struggled to compose herself.

53
00:02:40.277 --> 00:02:42.158
"Oh, it's nothing.

54
00:02:43.179 --> 00:02:44.540
Are you ready to go with me to Bill?"

55
00:02:45.521 --> 00:02:46.141
"What for?"

56
00:02:47.862 --> 00:02:49.684
Nancy avoided looking Oliver in the eye.

57
00:02:49.704 --> 00:02:52.185
"Oh, for no harm."

58
00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.287
"I don't believe it."

59
00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.808
"Fine, have it your way.

60
00:02:57.909 --> 00:02:58.750
For no good then."

61
00:02:59.891 --> 00:03:04.477
Suddenly she stooped over him and whispered, "I saved you from harm once, and I will again.

62
00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.378
This is not the time to try to escape.

63
00:03:08.399 --> 00:03:10.700
If you do, you may be the cause of my death.

64
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.281
Now come with me and be quiet."

65
00:03:14.421 --> 00:03:17.042
She held out her hand, and Oliver instinctively took it.

66
00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:21.484
A carriage was waiting outside the house, and they quickly climbed into it.

67
00:03:22.545 --> 00:03:26.546
Within a few minutes, they were at the house that Fagin had visited the previous evening.

68
00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:29.968
"So you've got the kid," said Sikes when they arrived.

69
00:03:30.924 --> 00:03:31.844
"Did he come quietly?"

70
00:03:31.864 --> 00:03:34.586
"Quiet as a lamb," said Nancy.

71
00:03:34.606 --> 00:03:40.008
"Good." He pulled off Oliver's cap and threw it into a corner.

72
00:03:41.089 --> 00:03:45.351
Then taking Oliver by the shoulder, he sat down at the table and stood the boy in front

73
00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:45.631
of him.

74
00:03:45.651 --> 00:03:52.154
"If you speak a word when you're out with me Sikes went on to threaten Oliver, who winced

75
00:03:52.214 --> 00:03:53.354
as he tried not to listen.

76
00:03:54.455 --> 00:03:57.236
He didn't need to hear the words to know that his life was in danger.

77
00:03:58.416 --> 00:04:01.557
Oliver didn't have much appetite for supper and went to bed soon after.

78
00:04:02.577 --> 00:04:04.818
The next morning Nancy called him at five o'clock.

79
00:04:05.898 --> 00:04:07.719
Rain was beating against the windowpanes.

80
00:04:08.879 --> 00:04:11.620
After a quick breakfast, Sikes and Oliver headed out.

81
00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.182
They were on the road all day, traveling on foot and by wagon for more than 25 miles.

82
00:04:18.362 --> 00:04:21.783
By seven o'clock that night, they stood before a ruined and decayed house.

83
00:04:23.023 --> 00:04:24.764
It was dark and appeared uninhabited.

84
00:04:26.456 --> 00:04:29.718
But Sikes opened the door and found Toby Crackit sitting by the fire.

85
00:04:29.738 --> 00:04:32.439
"Bill, I'm glad to see you!"

86
00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:33.340
said Crackit.

87
00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.621
"I was afraid you'd given up.

88
00:04:36.622 --> 00:04:37.422
But who's this?"

89
00:04:37.442 --> 00:04:42.445
"One of Fagin's boys," said Sikes, pulling a chair toward the fire.

90
00:04:42.465 --> 00:04:44.946
"What an innocent face!"

91
00:04:45.407 --> 00:04:46.067
said Crackit.

92
00:04:47.188 --> 00:04:50.149
"That'll be invaluable for picking old ladies' pockets at church."

93
00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:52.010
"Enough of that.

94
00:04:53.131 --> 00:04:54.452
Give us something to eat and drink.

95
00:04:55.572 --> 00:04:56.953
It'll soon be time to go out again."

96
00:04:57.953 --> 00:05:01.855
The men ate heartily, but Oliver could only force down a small crust of bread.

97
00:05:02.855 --> 00:05:04.556
Then they all dozed in front of the fire.

98
00:05:05.636 --> 00:05:08.638
Suddenly Toby Crackit declared it was half past one o'clock.

99
00:05:09.818 --> 00:05:13.039
In an instant Sikes jumped up and began preparations to go out.

100
00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:19.202
Wrapping themselves in large scarves and heavy overcoats, they gathered up an odd assortment of tools.

101
00:05:21.023 --> 00:05:23.624
The two robbers went out the door with Oliver between them.

102
00:05:24.712 --> 00:05:26.093
It was now intensely dark.

103
00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:31.996
The fog was heavy, and the air was so cold and damp that Oliver's hair and eyebrows froze.

104
00:05:33.077 --> 00:05:35.778
They passed through the town of Chertsey and turned up a road.

105
00:05:36.939 --> 00:05:39.100
Soon they came to a house surrounded by a wall.

106
00:05:40.121 --> 00:05:43.283
Crackit went over first, and then Sikes gave Oliver a boost.

107
00:05:44.463 --> 00:05:48.666
And now, for the first time, Oliver realized that they were going to rob the house.

108
00:05:49.947 --> 00:05:52.048
Filled with terror, he sank to his knees.

109
00:05:53.328 --> 00:05:54.468
"Oh, let me go!"

110
00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:55.389
he pleaded.

111
00:05:55.409 --> 00:05:58.570
"I'll never come near London, never, never!

112
00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.690
Have mercy on me and don't make me steal."

113
00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.091
"Get up!"

114
00:06:03.471 --> 00:06:05.151
muttered Sikes, trembling with rage.

115
00:06:05.171 --> 00:06:07.552
"And do what I tell you."

116
00:06:08.552 --> 00:06:12.493
They crept toward the back of the house, where a little window was covered by a shutter.

117
00:06:14.214 --> 00:06:19.215
While Crackit used a crowbar to pry off the shutter, Sikes whispered instructions in Oliver's ear.

118
00:06:20.335 --> 00:06:24.421
His job was to go through the window, walk along a hallway to the front of the house,

119
00:06:24.841 --> 00:06:26.862
and open the door for Sikes and Crackit.

120
00:06:27.902 --> 00:06:31.184
Sikes boosted Oliver up to the window and handed him a lantern.

121
00:06:31.204 --> 00:06:33.405
"Here, take this light."

122
00:06:34.605 --> 00:06:36.106
Oliver landed in a small room.

123
00:06:37.286 --> 00:06:39.127
Up ahead he could see a flight of stairs.

124
00:06:40.327 --> 00:06:43.909
And suddenly he decided to warn the inhabitants, no matter what happened to him.

125
00:06:45.049 --> 00:06:46.770
He started to run toward the stairs.

126
00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.251
"Wait!" called Sikes.

127
00:06:49.271 --> 00:06:50.972
"Come back!"

128
00:06:52.112 --> 00:06:54.614
Startled, Oliver dropped the lantern with a loud clatter.

129
00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.355
"Who's that?"

130
00:06:56.736 --> 00:06:57.416
called a voice.

131
00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:01.879
A vision of two men at the top of the stairs swam before Oliver's eyes.

132
00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:06.443
Then one of them fired a gun, and Oliver fell, wounded.
